// `it` means the subject ONLY inside a contract bracket. A written `requires` names the value it is
// about, because there is no bracket to say which one that would be — so `it` there is an ordinary
// identifier that nothing declared.
//
// This is the half of Decision 2 that keeps `it` from being a keyword: outside the one position
// where it has a meaning, the name is free, and `let it: Int = 7;` is a legal program.
function fee(amount: Decimal<2>) -> Decimal<2>
    requires it > $0.00
{
    return amount;
}
print(fee($5.00));
